{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1466905-questions-about-primal-glory-contract","id":1466905,"title":"Questions about Primal Glory Contract","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-11-05T23:06:51-07:00","id":1466905,"title":"Questions about Primal Glory Contract","content":"What exactly counts as damage inflicted by the chosen element? I get fire, because being on fire burns you for damage, but what about earth, air, and water? If you choose earth and someone throws a rock at you will that do damage? Technically the rock isn't doing the damage, it's the kinetic force of the throw. It's the same type of damage as being punched in the face. Does metal count as &quot;earth&quot;? Can you become immune to all metal weapons just by using this Contract? Does choosing water make you immune to drowning because technically drowning doesn't actually do damage (I think. I can't actually find the rules for drowing, if there even are any)?<br /> <br /> Also, is halving magical damage done before or after armour is subtracted?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-08T14:34:46-08:00","id":1467197,"title":"","content":"First of all, elemental in changeling can be a lot of things. It can be 'metal', it can be 'wood, or 'sunlight' or 'lightning' etc. Being immune to earth does not make you immune to metal, but being immune to metal does, at which point a steel sword would deal no damage to you. I always assumed that the damage was halved before any other modifiers (such as armor), but that's a call for the ST to make depending on their interpretation. I'd say that making yourself immune to water damage wouldn't allow you to breathe underwater, but again, other STs might rule this differently (a case could definitely be made for it).<br /> <br /> Some weapons would be made of specific elements (bone, glass, wood, steel, etc), and some elements will deal damage just for being in touch to them (fire, lava, acid, etc). As for the rest? You'll probably only make yourself immune to Air if someone's got a Hedgespun sword made of the Northern Wind or if they've invoked the Elemental Weapon to grab a lance out of the air surrounding them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12103,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12103-vintervalpen","user":"Vintervalpen","date":". 11-08-2021, 05:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12103-vintervalpen","name":"Vintervalpen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-11T13:05:05-08:00","id":1467467,"title":"","content":"So, if a creature made of stone punches someone that had used Primal Glory to become immune/resistant to earth, would Primal Glory apply? Technically it's not the earth that's doing damage, it's the force of the punch. Or is that being too nitpicky for an rpg?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-11T13:42:46-08:00","id":1467473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowdragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1466905-questions-about-primal-glory-contract?p=1467467#post1467467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or is that being too nitpicky for an rpg?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably, this.<br /> <br /> Some games, like D&amp;D, have a clear rule for damage type based on source and then it is more direct to define those things. But that's not how CtL work for several reasons, and so it isn't reasonable to be too specific on how this source works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-12T04:00:20-08:00","id":1467534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowdragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1466905-questions-about-primal-glory-contract?p=1467467#post1467467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, if a creature made of stone punches someone that had used Primal Glory to become immune/resistant to earth, would Primal Glory apply? Technically it's not the earth that's doing damage, it's the force of the punch. Or is that being too nitpicky for an rpg?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see why you're extending earth to stone or metals. Stone is an &quot;earthy&quot; material, sure, but if you pick earth as the element to become immune to, it should probably only affect damage that comes from things made out of soil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-12T16:24:50-08:00","id":1467609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1466905-questions-about-primal-glory-contract?p=1467534#post1467534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't see why you're extending earth to stone or metals. Stone is an &quot;earthy&quot; material, sure, but if you pick earth as the element to become immune to, it should probably only affect damage that comes from things made out of soil.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ok, fine, a creature made of living soil. Or drinking water to become immune to a creature made out of water. How specific do we need to get when defining an element? Does it have to be distilled water to count as water? Since tap water has other stuff in it, like flouride, does it not count as water any more and can therefore bypass Primal Fury? Do we have to distinguish between salt water, fresh water, tap water, etc?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-12T17:07:52-08:00","id":1467615,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s more art, and less science. <br /> <br /> I personally go with Final Fantasy/Dragon Quest-esque logic for things like this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-12T18:44:34-08:00","id":1467624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowdragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1466905-questions-about-primal-glory-contract?p=1467609#post1467609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Ok, fine, a creature made of living soil. Or drinking water to become immune to a creature made out of water. How specific do we need to get when defining an element? Does it have to be distilled water to count as water? Since tap water has other stuff in it, like flouride, does it not count as water any more and can therefore bypass Primal Fury? Do we have to distinguish between salt water, fresh water, tap water, etc?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Is it more fun or better rewards the player who bought the power and is using it?&quot; is my general guideline to such things.<br /> <br /> I know that if I bought the contract with water and the GM tried to get into &quot;Wait, did you mean salt water or fresh water?&quot;, I'd have a lot to look askance over.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-12T19:42:19-08:00","id":1467627,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the best bottom line is that the player should feel the power is useful. If the player feels like the point was wasted, then it is better to just be less picky.<br /> <br /> And I do think differentiating stone from earth when it comes to it will probably feel a lot more like being cheated by the ST, unless sources of damage made of soil are enough of a thing in a given chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-12T20:37:32-08:00","id":1467635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1466905-questions-about-primal-glory-contract?p=1467627#post1467627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I do think differentiating stone from earth when it comes to it will probably feel a lot more like being cheated by the ST, unless sources of damage made of soil are enough of a thing in a given chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Animate a piece of the local environment, which has natural advantages based on what it's made of&quot; is a Common Contract. Flippant fine-slicing aside, I'm going to distinguish if you're dealing with a Rock-type or a Ground-type, for much the same reason as I'm going to distinguish between running in mud and on concrete.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 11-12-2021, 11:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-13T02:12:51-08:00","id":1467665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowdragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1466905-questions-about-primal-glory-contract?p=1467609#post1467609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Ok, fine, a creature made of living soil. Or drinking water to become immune to a creature made out of water. How specific do we need to get when defining an element? Does it have to be distilled water to count as water? Since tap water has other stuff in it, like flouride, does it not count as water any more and can therefore bypass Primal Fury? Do we have to distinguish between salt water, fresh water, tap water, etc?</div> </div> </div> </div>Stone and soil, two different materials with different compositions and different qualities, are definitely comparable to the differences between salt water, fresh water, and tap water since they only share almost all the same qualities and have as much as miniscule differences in composition.<br /> <br /> If someone uses Primal Glory against &quot;earth&quot;, I do think it's reasonable to include impurities such as pebbles, half-decayed plant matter, and even composting life forms, since they're something you'd naturally include if you animated a patch of soil, but assuming minerals and metals are generally included means you've covered just about all solid substances that aren't organic. That's a massive overreach and massively imbalanced compared to &quot;fire&quot; or &quot;electricity&quot;, or even elemental groupings like &quot;acids&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}